1
00:00:00,140 --> 00:00:02,480
 Now that we covered all the main conceptual

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,150
 aspects of the Android system, let's look at how

3
00:00:05,150 --> 00:00:08,900
 these aspects work in practice through a demo.

4
00:00:08,900 --> 00:00:12,220
 Let's start our Android demo by downloading the Android

5
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:17,000
 SDK, which will allow us to build Android apps. To do that, we need to go to

6
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:22,300
 the site developer.android.com. Here, we click on Develop.

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:25,270
 Then we click on Tools. And finally, we click

8
00:00:25,270 --> 00:00:28,310
 on Download here on the left. This brings us to

9
00:00:28,310 --> 00:00:31,780
 this page in which we can get the Android SDK. And

10
00:00:31,780 --> 00:00:34,490
 we can get it as a bundle, where the bundle

11
00:00:34,490 --> 00:00:38,209
 includes various things such as the Eclipse IDE, plus the ADT

12
00:00:38,209 --> 00:00:42,520
 plugin, Android SDK Tools and other parts. So for now,

13
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:45,060
 what we're going to do, we're just going to download the Android SDK.

14
00:00:45,060 --> 00:00:47,450
 So we're going to skip that and we're going to go to DOWNLOAD

15
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:50,970
 FOR OTHER PLATFORMS. And here where it says SDK Tools Only,

16
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:54,060
 you can pick the version of the Android SDK for your platform.

17
00:00:54,060 --> 00:00:55,980
 So if you work on a Mac, you will pick this one

18
00:00:55,980 --> 00:00:59,600
 and, otherwise, you can pick the Linux version or the Windows version.

19
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:02,490
 And once you click on that, you will get the SDK package.

20
00:01:02,490 --> 00:01:05,880
 Now that you have downloaded the Android SDK for your platform, you

21
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:09,240
 can unzip it and you can do that graphically or as I'm

22
00:01:09,240 --> 00:01:13,400
 doing here from the command line. So I'm just going to run unzip

23
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:16,080
 and pass the file as a parameter. And I'm doing the command

24
00:01:16,080 --> 00:01:18,430
 line version because that's, you know, a little more

25
00:01:18,430 --> 00:01:21,130
 challenging so the, the GUI one, you'll basically just click

26
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:24,145
 on the archive. And as soon as we have unpacked

27
00:01:24,145 --> 00:01:28,320
 the SDK, we can move into the android-sdk directory. We

28
00:01:28,320 --> 00:01:32,075
 can look at the content of the directory. And as

29
00:01:32,075 --> 00:01:36,180
 you can see, there are several files and directories inside.

30
00:01:36,180 --> 00:01:38,200
 And the one that we're interested in right now is

31
00:01:38,200 --> 00:01:42,340
 the tools directory. So that's where we're going to go next.

32
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:45,084
 And again, if you're doing this through a GUI, we'll just click

33
00:01:45,084 --> 00:01:48,550
 on the tools directory. And here, we have a bunch of applications. These

34
00:01:48,550 --> 00:01:51,570
 are all part of the Android SDK. And what we're interested in is

35
00:01:51,570 --> 00:01:54,995
 this android command. So we're going to run it, which you can do again

36
00:01:54,995 --> 00:01:57,500
 from the command line or just by clicking on it. You'll probably

37
00:01:57,500 --> 00:01:59,680
 get an error here but don't worry about it. We're going to fix it

38
00:01:59,680 --> 00:02:02,310
 in a minute. So when we run the command, we're going to get the

39
00:02:02,310 --> 00:02:04,710
 Android SDK Manager, which allows us

40
00:02:04,710 --> 00:02:07,340
 to manage the different packages

41
00:02:07,340 --> 00:02:09,150
 that are part of the Android SDK so to

42
00:02:09,150 --> 00:02:12,720
 see which ones are installed and to install new ones. And

43
00:02:12,720 --> 00:02:15,480
 as you can see, you can install different versions

44
00:02:15,480 --> 00:02:18,640
 of Android. And for each version, there is a corresponding

45
00:02:18,640 --> 00:02:22,005
 API version. And you can also see that the,

46
00:02:22,005 --> 00:02:24,910
 the one selected by default is the latest version, which,

47
00:02:24,910 --> 00:02:28,975
 in this case, is Android 4.4 and API version

48
00:02:28,975 --> 00:02:32,850
 19. So all the corresponding parts are selected for installation

49
00:02:32,850 --> 00:02:36,100
 and, similarly, the platform tools and the build tools are also

50
00:02:36,100 --> 00:02:38,710
 selected. And you can see on the right that none of

51
00:02:38,710 --> 00:02:42,460
 these packages is currently installed. So we click Install to install

52
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:46,490
 these nine packages. Next, we have to accept the license in

53
00:02:46,490 --> 00:02:48,530
 order to be able to install the packages. So we do

54
00:02:48,530 --> 00:02:51,950
 that. We click Install again. And if you want, you can

55
00:02:51,950 --> 00:02:54,440
 also look at the log here to see what's happening during

56
00:02:54,440 --> 00:02:58,410
 the installation. And you can see that there's an error there referring

57
00:02:58,410 --> 00:02:59,940
 to the fact that, you know, stopping

58
00:02:59,940 --> 00:03:02,290
 the ADB server failed and that's okay because

59
00:03:02,290 --> 00:03:04,110
 we haven't installed the server yet. So

60
00:03:04,110 --> 00:03:06,261
 you might see exactly the same error. And

61
00:03:06,261 --> 00:03:09,081
 at this point, you know, just you know, you just have to wait until the

62
00:03:09,081 --> 00:03:11,990
 installation finishes. So we're going to stop here

63
00:03:11,990 --> 00:03:11,990
 and we're going to go to the next step.

